# Dreadmaw's Ire needs an attacking creature (CR 508.1k): in the first main phase, with Mother of Runes not yet attacking,
# the spell has no legal target and is not offered (the refusal). Mother attacks, Bot2's Ornithopter blocks, and after
# blockers the Ire makes Mother a 3/3 trampler: two damage to the 0/2 Ornithopter, one tramples over to Bot2, and that
# combat damage to a player triggers "destroy target artifact that player controls" - Bot1's own Mox Ruby is not a
# candidate (the refusal) while Bot2's Sol Ring and Mox Jet are; the Sol Ring is chosen and the Jet survives.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Pearl
Mox Ruby
Mother of Runes
Dreadmaw's Ire
Plains x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Jet
Sol Ring
Ornithopter
Island x12

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Mother of Runes.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
! Bot1.Hand.Dreadmaw's Ire.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Mother of Runes)
Bot1.Attack(Mother of Runes > Bot2)
Bot2.Block(Ornithopter > Mother of Runes)
[T3 Bot1.Blockers]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dreadmaw's Ire.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Mother of Runes)
! Bot1.Target(Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Sol Ring)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Jet
Bot2.Graveyard = Sol Ring; Ornithopter
Bot1.Battlefield.Mother of Runes.Power = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Mother of Runes.Keywords = Trample
